 PROCEDURE CODE
572-BIS
Without prejudice to the special jurisdiction conferred on the Justice of the Peace [4 and on the Youth Court, in the context of youth protection measures,]4 and to special legislation, the Family Court hears:
1¡ applications relating to personal status, including applications relating to Belgian nationality and recognition of stateless status [5 , without prejudice to the jurisdiction conferred on the criminal court by Article 391octies of the Criminal Code and Article 79quater of the Act of 15 December 1980 on the entry, residence, establishment and removal of foreign nationals]5;]3
 2¡ applications relating to the annulment of legal cohabitation and appeals against the refusal of the civil registrar to record the declaration of legal cohabitation]2 without prejudice to the jurisdiction conferred on the criminal court by article 391octies of the Criminal Code and article 79quater of the law of 15 December 1980 on access to the territory, residence, settlement and removal of foreign nationals;
3¡ applications from spouses and legal cohabitants relating to the exercise of their rights or to their property and the provisional measures relating thereto;
4¡ applications relating to the exercise of parental authority, accommodation or contact rights in respect of minor children;]2
5¡ findings that it is permanently impossible to exercise parental authority as referred to in article 389 of the Civil Code;
6¡ claims referred to In article 1322bis;
7¡ claims relating to maintenance obligations;
8¡ disputes relating to the determination of the recipient(s) of family allowances for children whose parents no longer live together, as well as applications to oppose payment to the recipient;
9¡ applications relating to matrimonial property regimes]2 , succession, gifts inter vivos or wills;
10¡ applications for partition;
11¡ applications relating to the temporary ban on residence referred to in the Act of 15 May 2012 relating to the temporary ban on residence in the event of domestic violence;
12¡ opposition made by the holder of parental authority to the exercise of the rights of a minor child who has not been emancipated to the withdrawal of sums entered in the latter's passbook or savings account;
13¡ requests made pursuant to Article 220, ¤ 3, of the Civil Code;
14¡ opposition to payment to the recipient of the family benefits referred to in Article 69 , of the laws relating to family benefits for salaried employees coordinated on 19 December 1939, except where the Youth Court has been seised on the basis of Article 29 of the law of 8 April 1965 relating to the protection of young people, the care of minors who have committed an offence and compensation for the damage caused by that offence, and except where the Justice of the Peace has jurisdiction by virtue of Article 594, 8¡;
15¡ opposition to the payment to the recipient of family benefits for self-employed persons, as referred to in Article 31, ¤ 3, of the Royal Decree of 8 April 1976 establishing the system of family benefits for self-employed persons, except where the Youth Court has been seised on the basis of Article 29 of the Law of 8 April 1965 on the protection of young people, the care of minors who have committed an act classified as an offence and compensation for the damage caused by that act, and except where the Justice of the Peace has jurisdiction by virtue of Article 594, 9¡.
